  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internews: F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkning av landsbygdsradio i 3R-DRC (2022-2025)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internews: Reinforcing Rural Radios in 3R-DRC (2022 - 2025)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the lessons learnt, success and impact of the first phase of the project between November 2019 to August 2022 and aiming to keep working in synergy with the USA and Swiss under MSDA project, Internews proposes the Reinforcing Rural Radios in DRC (3R-DRC) project with the aim of continuing under the same framework, with slightly refined objectives, for a period of 36 months. Having noted the information dynamics in the country and in rural areas as well as the need for holistic support, the second phase of the project will focus more on remote, underserved locations where audience reach is still a problem and where the marginalisation of women and youth is more acute. The second phase aims to broaden and scale up the impacts and achievements from the first phase to sustain partners&#x2019; capacity and actions and secure more long-term effects in a conducive context where the government appears to exhibit political will in adopting reforms and addressing governance issues.

The 3R-DRC project will focus on the following provinces where Internews and local partners have established strong presence, networks and activities (Most of the provinces were covered during the first phase of the programme): Kongo Central, Sud Kivu, Kasai, Kasai Central, Kasai Oriental, Haut Katanga, Lualaba, Tshopo, Haut Uele, Bas Uele, Equateur and Kinshasa.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Med utg&#xe5;ngspunkt i erfarenheterna, framg&#xe5;ngarna och effekterna av projektets f&#xf6;rsta fas mellan november 2019 och augusti 2022 och i syfte att forts&#xe4;tta att arbeta i synergi med USA och Schweiz inom ramen f&#xf6;r MSDA-projektet f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;r Internews projektet Reinforcing Rural Radios in DRC (3R-DRC) i syfte att forts&#xe4;tta inom samma ram, med n&#xe5;got mer detaljerade m&#xe5;l, under en period p&#xe5; 36 m&#xe5;nader. Efter att ha noterat informationsdynamiken i landet och p&#xe5; landsbygden samt behovet av holistiskt st&#xf6;d kommer projektets andra fas att inriktas mer p&#xe5; avl&#xe4;gsna och underf&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjda platser d&#xe4;r det fortfarande &#xe4;r sv&#xe5;rt att n&#xe5; ut till publiken och d&#xe4;r marginaliseringen av kvinnor och ungdomar &#xe4;r mer akut. Syftet med den andra fasen &#xe4;r att bredda och skala upp effekterna och resultaten fr&#xe5;n den f&#xf6;rsta fasen f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja partnernas kapacitet och &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder och s&#xe4;kra mer l&#xe5;ngsiktiga effekter i ett gynnsamt sammanhang d&#xe4;r regeringen verkar visa politisk vilja att anta reformer och ta itu med fr&#xe5;gor som r&#xf6;r styrelseformer.

3R-DRC-projektet kommer att fokusera p&#xe5; f&#xf6;ljande provinser d&#xe4;r Internews och lokala partner har etablerat stark n&#xe4;rvaro, n&#xe4;tverk och verksamhet (de flesta av provinserna t&#xe4;cktes under programmets f&#xf6;rsta fas): Kongo Central, Sud Kivu, Kasai, Kasai Central, Kasai Oriental, Haut Katanga, Lualaba, Tshopo, Haut Uele, Bas Uele, Equateur och Kinshasa.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this intervention is to promote a more open and vibrant community radio sector that meets the information needs of citizens in rural areas (with a focus on women and youth) and strengthens their participation in public debate.

Internews and its local partners will achieve this through the following intermediate results:

1. Improve the legal framework and the capacity to protect journalists for rural community radios with media reforms and safeguarding mechanisms

2. Improve the business and financial sustainability of rural radio stations 

3. Increase the quantity, quality and reach of rural radio content on democracy and  human rights, electoral education and SGBV.</narrative>
  </description>
